  "id": "COMPOUND:34435 - PROTEIN:5753",
  "verbalization": "Ent-Gloeosteretriol appears to have a potential relationship with OVCAR through multiple distinct pathways, all of which involve the modulation of downstream targets. The first pathway links Ent-Gloeosteretriol to Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK, which is then targeted by Oblonganoside C, ultimately leading to OVCAR. The second pathway connects Ent-Gloeosteretriol to DMS-53, which is targeted by Gerontoisoflavone A, also resulting in OVCAR. The third pathway involves Ent-Gloeosteretriol targeting Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 11, which is inhibited by methohexital, again leading to OVCAR. These findings suggest that Ent-Gloeosteretriol may exert its effects on OVCAR through various molecular mechanisms, potentially involving kinase inhibition or signaling modulation. The consistent involvement of OVCAR in multiple pathways indicates a possible role in tumor progression or survival, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Ent-Gloeosteretriol and OVCAR, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the biological relevance of these interactions.",
